+ ### 2. Get testnet DASH
+ Visit the Dash testnet faucet at https://testnet-faucet.dash.org/ to receive free testnet DASH for Platform operations.
+ ### 3. Create a Platform Identity
+ # Using the Dash SDK or Platform console, create an identity:
+ # See https://docs.dash.org/en/stable/docs/tutorials/identities-and-names.html
+ This registers your identity on the Dash Platform testnet and returns an Identity ID (base58 string).
+ ### 4. Top up credits
+ Your identity needs Platform credits to submit documents. Top up via the SDK:
+ # Top up credits using your identity and funded wallet
+ # See https://docs.dash.org/en/stable/docs/tutorials/identities-and-names.html#top-up-an-identity
+ ### 5. Set environment variables
+ export CRITICAL_WIF="your-testnet-WIF-private-key"
+ export DASHPASS_IDENTITY_ID="your-platform-identity-id"
+ # Optional: deploy your own contract and set this
+ # export DASHPASS_CONTRACT_ID="your-contract-id"
+ ### 6. First put/get
+ # Store a credential
+ echo "my-secret-value" | node dashpass-cli.mjs put \
+   --service test-service \
+   --type api-key \
+   --level normal \
+   --label "Test credential" \
+   --value-stdin
+ # Retrieve it
+ node dashpass-cli.mjs get --service test-service
+ ### 7. (Optional) Deploy your own contract
+ The default shared testnet contract works for testing. For production use, deploy your own contract using `dashpass-vault-v2-contract.json` and set `DASHPASS_CONTRACT_ID`.

